0 Die Klemme, 1958 - three 2 x 2 bricks WITH the tube (A3-S04b)
0 Name: klemme.ldr
0 Author: spex project (hand-authored placement data; not sourced from an official ldraw.org models/ release)
0 // The official 3003.dat, tube and all. The three bricks before this one in
0 // the act are the same shell with the tube removed, so the clutch is
0 // something that ARRIVES in 1958 rather than something that was always
0 // there - which is the correction this shot exists to make.
0 //
0 // THE ONE AUTHORED DEPARTURE FROM REAL LDRAW GEOMETRY IN THE PIECE.
0 // LDraw's stud outer diameter and tube inner diameter are both nominally
0 // 12 LDU and interpenetrate exactly: in a correctly stacked model the stud
0 // and the tube occupy the same cylinder and nothing can be SEEN entering
0 // anything. That is right for a model and useless for a macro whose whole
0 // subject is the entering. So the top brick is lifted 6 LDU (2.4 mm) - a
0 // quarter of a course, off the grid on purpose - and a transform track on
0 // klemme/3003/2 seats it over the shot. A starting condition the shot
0 // resolves, not a permanent lie about the geometry.
0 //
0 // Seated positions, LDraw +Y down, brick 24 LDU tall:
0 //   course 0  y = -24
0 //   course 1  y = -48
0 //   course 2  y = -72   <- authored here as -78
0 //
0 // Stage position x = 21200 LDU (1060 studs).
1 15 21200 -24 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3003.dat
1 15 21200 -48 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3003.dat
1 15 21200 -78 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3003.dat
